Package: reach.rate
Title: Fit, Diagnose, and Apply Hydrometric Rating Curves
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Jonathan", "Payne", , "jonathan.payne1988@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Tools for fitting multi-limb power-law stage-discharge rating
    curves by nonlinear least squares, diagnosing fit quality (including
    leverage/influence and closed-form or bootstrap coefficient
    uncertainty), detecting and resolving discontinuities ("junction gaps")
    between independently-fitted limbs, converting a fitted rating into a
    discharge time series, and documenting rating amendments. Includes a
    segmented joint-model parameterisation after Hodson et al. (2024),
    opt-in age-based recency weighting for gaugings, and versioned ratings
    for stations that have been re-rated over time. Beyond gauging-based
    fitting, also derives a rating from a surveyed cross-section alone via
    Manning's equation, and computes discharge for standard weir and flume
    structures (rectangular, V-notch, Cipoletti, Parshall flume) from their
    own published equations with GUM-style propagated uncertainty. Fitted
    ratings are represented as 'S7' classes that carry their own gaugings,
    fitting bookkeeping, and provenance, so a rating is never separated
    from the data and assumptions that produced it.
